## Context Focus

- Prioritize files under `src/app/**`, `src/components/**`, `src/lib/**`, `src/models/**`, `src/types/**`, and `src/hooks/**`.
- De-prioritize large assets under `public/**` and any generated artifacts (`.next`, `dist`, `coverage`).

## Path Aliases

- Use `@/` to reference `src/` (e.g., `@/lib/mongoose`, `@/components/ui/button`).

## API Route Patterns (Next.js App Router)

- Handlers live in `src/app/api/**/route.ts` and export HTTP methods.
- Authentication:
  - Server Components: use `createReadOnlyClient()` for read-only auth context.
  - API Routes / Server Actions: use `createClient()` for full read/write.
  - Server-only ops: use `supabaseAdmin` (service role) and never expose to client.
- Error handling: return `NextResponse.json({ error }, { status })` with clear codes.

## Data Architecture

- MongoDB Atlas stores raw conversations/messages.
- Supabase (Postgres) stores aggregated insights, metrics, and auth.
- Common utilities:
  - `@/lib/mongoose` for Mongo connection (ensure connection before queries).
  - `@/lib/mongo` for health/index utilities.
  - `@/lib/supabase/*` for Supabase client helpers.

## UI Component Conventions

- Styling: TailwindCSS + `@shadcn/ui`.
- Prefer Shadcn components for inputs, dialogs, tables, date-picker.
- Loading state: `Skeleton`; Error state: `Alert`; purposeful empty state with CTA.

## Realtime & Jobs

- Pusher for realtime UI updates.
- Upstash Queue for background jobs and retries (cron and processing).

## Internationalization

- `next-intl` via `src/i18n/request.ts`; messages in `messages/*.json`.
- Supported locales: `en`, `ru`, `kz`.

## Security & Quality

- Validate inputs on API boundaries; add rate limiting where appropriate.
- Avoid leaking secrets to the client; use service role only on server.
- TypeScript: prefer explicit function signatures for exported APIs.

## Notes for Assistants

- When editing code, keep imports aligned with the alias and project structure.
- Avoid introducing new libraries unless necessary; follow existing patterns.
- Prefer incremental edits that match the current style and formatting.
